This class stores items by ID, supports adding quantities, removing quantities, and calculating the total price.

# ShoppingCart Class in PHP

Here's a clean implementation of a `ShoppingCart` class with the requested methods:

```php
<?php

class ShoppingCart
{
    /**
     * @var array<string, array{price: float, quantity: int}>
     */
    private array $items = [];

    /**
     * Add an item to the cart. If it already exists, increase its quantity.
     *
     * @param string $name     Unique identifier for the item
     * @param float  $price    Price per unit
     * @param int    $quantity Number of units to add
     * @throws InvalidArgumentException
     */
    public function addItem(string $name, float $price, int $quantity = 1): void
    {
        if ($price < 0) {
            throw new InvalidArgumentException('Price cannot be negative.');
        }
        if ($quantity < 1) {
            throw new InvalidArgumentException('Quantity must be at least 1.');
        }

        if (isset($this->items[$name])) {
            $this->items[$name]['quantity'] += $quantity;
        } else {
            $this->items[$name] = [
                'price'    => $price,
                'quantity' => $quantity,
            ];
        }
    }

    /**
     * Remove an item from the cart.
     *
     * @param string $name
     * @param int|null $quantity  Remove only this many units; null removes all.
     * @return bool  True if something was removed, false otherwise.
     */
    public function removeItem(string $name, ?int $quantity = null): bool
    {
        if (!isset($this->items[$name])) {
            return false;
        }

        if ($quantity === null || $quantity >= $this->items[$name]['quantity']) {
            unset($this->items[$name]);
        } else {
            $this->items[$name]['quantity'] -= $quantity;
        }

        return true;
    }

    /**
     * Get the total cost of all items in the cart.
     */
    public function getTotal(): float
    {
        $total = 0.0;

        foreach ($this->items as $item) {
            $total += $item['price'] * $item['quantity'];
        }

        return round($total, 2);
    }

    /**
     * Optional: return the current items (useful for display/testing).
     */
    public function getItems(): array
    {
        return $this->items;
    }
}
```

