| Step | Why |
|------|-----|
| **Transliteration** | Turns `é`, `ñ`, `ü`, etc. into ASCII so the slug stays readable in any browser. Uses ICU if available, `iconv` as fallback. |
| **`mb_strtolower`** | Multibyte-safe lowercasing (plain `strtolower` mangles UTF-8). |
| **`\p{L}\p{Nd}` with `/u`** | Keeps letters and digits from *any* Unicode script (Cyrillic, Greek, CJK, etc.), not just `[a-z0-9]`. |
| **Collapse + trim** | Prevents `hello---world-` style output. |
| **Configurable separator** | Some systems prefer `_` or `.`. |

## Optional Enhancements

If you want to **strip non-ASCII entirely** (e.g. force an English-only slug), replace step 4 with:

```php
$string = preg_replace('/[^a-z0-9]+/', $separator, $string);
```

If you need **unique slugs** (avoiding DB collisions), wrap it like:

```php
function uniqueSlug(string $title, callable $exists): string
{
    $base = slugify($title) ?: 'item';
    $slug = $base;
    $i = 2;
    while ($exists($slug)) {
        $slug = $base . '-' . $i++;
    }
    return $slug;
}

// Example:
$slug = uniqueSlug('Hello World', fn($s) => (bool) $pdo
    ->query("SELECT 1 FROM posts WHERE slug = " . $pdo->quote($s))
    ->fetchColumn());
```

