## Unicode-aware version (keeps non-Latin scripts)

If you want slugs like `日本語` or `привет` instead of empty strings, use the `u` modifier and allow any Unicode letter/number:

```php
function slugify(string $string, string $separator = '-'): string
{
    $string = trim($string);

    // Optional: transliterate Latin accents (ä -> a) but keep other scripts intact
    $transliterated = iconv('UTF-8', 'ASCII//TRANSLIT//IGNORE', $string);
    if ($transliterated !== false && $transliterated !== '') {
        $string = $transliterated;
    }

    $string = mb_strtolower($string, 'UTF-8');

    // Replace any run of characters that is not a letter/number with the separator
    $pattern = '/[^\p{L}\p{N}]+/u';
    $string = preg_replace($pattern, $separator, $string) ?? $string;

    // Collapse repeated separators
    $string = preg_replace('/' . preg_quote($separator, '/') . '{2,}/u', $separator, $string) ?? $string;

    return trim($string, $separator);
}
```

```php
slugify('Привет Мир');   // "привет-мир"
slugify('日本語のタイトル'); // "日本語のタイトル"
```

