- **Unicode slugs:** if you want to keep non-Latin characters (e.g. `你好`), replace step 4 with `preg_replace('/[^\p{L}\p{N}]+/u', '-', $string)` and skip the transliteration step.

## The function

```php
<?php

/**
 * Convert a title into a URL-safe slug.
 *
 * @param string $string    Text to slugify.
 * @param string $separator Character(s) used to join the words.
 * @return string
 */
function slugify(string $string, string $separator = '-'): string
{
    if ($separator === '') {
        $separator = '-';
    }

    $string = trim($string);

    // 1. Drop invalid UTF-8 byte sequences so the /u regexes below cannot fail.
    if (function_exists('mb_check_encoding') && !mb_check_encoding($string, 'UTF-8')) {
        $string = mb_convert_encoding($string, 'UTF-8', 'UTF-8');
    }

    // 2. Decompose accented characters (é -> e + U+0301) so the accent can be
    //    stripped while the base letter survives.
    if (class_exists('Normalizer')) {
        $normalized = \Normalizer::normalize($string, \Normalizer::FORM_D);
        if (is_string($normalized)) {
            $string = $normalized;
        }
    }

    // 3. Map characters that do *not* decompose into ASCII (ß, ø, æ, ł, đ, …).
    $string = strtr($string, slugify_transliterations());

    // 4. Remove the combining marks left over from step 2.
    $string = preg_replace('/\p{Mn}+/u', '', $string) ?? $string;

    // 5. Lowercase (multibyte aware when mbstring is available).
    $string = function_exists('mb_strtolower')
        ? mb_strtolower($string, 'UTF-8')
        : strtolower($string);

    // 6. Anything that is not an ASCII letter or digit becomes the separator.
    $string = preg_replace('/[^a-z0-9]+/u', $separator, $string);
    if ($string === null) {
        return '';
    }

    // 7. Collapse repeated separators and trim them from both ends.
    $quoted = preg_quote($separator, '/');
    $string = preg_replace('/' . $quoted . '{2,}/', $separator, $string);
