slugify('Café Über Straße');        // "cafe-uber-strasse"
slugify('  Multiple   Spaces  ');   // "multiple-spaces"
slugify('PHP & MySQL');             // "php-mysql"
slugify('100% Pure — Ünïcödé');     // "100-pure-unicode"
slugify('Hello World', '_');        // "hello_world"
```

### Notes

- The `+` in the regex collapses consecutive separators automatically, so no extra de-duplication step is needed.
- `trim()` removes leading/trailing separators left over from punctuation (e.g. `"Hello!"` → `"hello"`).
- If the result can be empty (e.g. `slugify('!!!')`), guard against it before inserting into the database.
- For high-traffic sites, cache the `Transliterator` object in a static variable instead of recreating it on every call:

```php
static $t = null;
$t ??= Transliterator::create('Any-Latin; Latin-ASCII; Lower()');
```

## The function

```php
/**
 * Convert a title into a URL-safe slug.
 *
 * @param string $string     Input title.
 * @param int    $maxLength  Max length of the result (0 = unlimited).
 * @param string $separator  Character used to join words.
 */
function slugify(string $string, int $maxLength = 0, string $separator = '-'): string
{
    // 1. Decompose unicode so accents become separate combining marks.
    if (class_exists('Normalizer')) {
        $normalized = \Normalizer::normalize($string, \Normalizer::FORM_D);
        if ($normalized !== false) {
            $string = $normalized;
        }
    }

    // 2. Map characters that have no sensible ASCII transliteration.
    static $map = [
        'ä' => 'ae', 'ö' => 'oe', 'ü' => 'ue', 'ß' => 'ss', 'æ' => 'ae',
        'œ' => 'oe', 'ø' => 'o',  'å' => 'a',  'đ' => 'd',  'ð' => 'd',
        'þ' => 'th', 'ł' => 'l',  'ħ' => 'h',  'ı' => 'i',  'ŋ' => 'ng',
    ];
    $string = strtr($string, $map);

    // 3. Transliterate anything still non-ASCII (é -> e, Cyrillic, etc.).
    $ascii = @iconv('UTF-8', 'ASCII//TRANSLIT//IGNORE', $string);
    if ($ascii !== false) {
        $string = $ascii;
    }

    // 4. Lowercase (multibyte-safe) and drop apostrophes: "don't" -> "dont".
    $string = mb_strtolower($string, 'UTF-8');
    $string = str_replace(["'", "\u{2019}"], '', $string);

    // 5. Replace every run of non-alphanumerics with the separator.
    $string = preg_replace('/[^a-z0-9]+/', $separator, $string);

    // 6. Trim leading/trailing separators and collapse repeats.
    $string = trim($string, $separator);
    $string = preg_replace('/' . preg_quote($separator, '/') . '{2,}/', $separator, $string);

    // 7. Optionally truncate on a word boundary.
    if ($maxLength > 0 && mb_strlen($string) > $maxLength) {
        $string = rtrim(mb_substr($string, 0, $maxLength, 'UTF-8'), $separator);
    }

    return $string;
}
```

